  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\left[\\mathrm{a}_{i j}\\right]$ be a $2 \\times 2$ matrix such that $\\mathrm{a}_{i j} \\in\\{0,1\\}$ for all $i$ and $j$. Let the random variable X denote the possible values of the determinant of the matrix $A$. Then, the variance of $X$ is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{8}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{8}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline x & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\\n\\hline P(x) & \\frac{10}{16} & \\frac{3}{16} & \\frac{3}{16} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\operatorname{Var}(x)=E\\left(x^2\\right)-[E(x)]^2 \\\\ & =\\sum_{i=1}^3 x_i^2 P\\left(x_i\\right)-(\\mu)^2 \\\\ & =1 \\times \\frac{3}{16}+1 \\times \\frac{3}{16} \\quad[\\mu=0] \\\\ & =\\frac{6}{16}=\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}